   6:   bars: 2 parallel full-interior lines of bar_color, either both rows (horizontal) or both cols (vertical)
   7:   gap: on_count cells between the two bars (range 1-4); filled with source_color on selected periodic slices
   8:   periodic_pattern:
   9:     axis: perpendicular to bars (rows if vertical bars, cols if horizontal)
  10:     unit: on_count consecutive 1s + off_count consecutive 0s (on 1-4, off 2-3, period = on+off = 3-6)
  11:     inner alignment: unit[0] at inner index 0 (grid index 1); pattern may truncate at far edge
  12:     source cells: on-slices between the two bars are filled with source_color; off-slices are bg
  13:   remaining_interior: bg (0) everywhere inside the frame not occupied by bars or source stripes
  14:   output_rule: |
  15:     Remove frame. Extend bars to span full grid axis. Infer periodic mask from inner source pattern,
  16:     extend it to full grid length (mask[i] = inner_unit[i % period] with offset 1 for the frame).
  17:     Selected rows/cols get frame_color everywhere (except bar/source cols/rows keep their color).
  18:     Non-selected rows/cols are bg. Source cells between bars on selected slices keep source_color.
